      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, why would you suggest 90210 and 90213? They already have high incomes and low crime. Isn't the whole point of \"social impact\" to help the areas that are actually struggling? It feels like you're just recommending money go to places that are already doing well. Why is being \"receptive to initiatives\" based on the racial makeup more important than, say, reducing the high crime in 90211?",
